{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00668",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 1.18,
      "end_seconds": 12.63,
      "duration_seconds": 11.45,
      "text": "Hi, sorry, I'm Becky, Oliver's mum, and this is Gran, who has him after school. It's his bowels, he's not been going."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.95,
      "end_seconds": 20.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "Hello both, hello Oliver. How old are you, Oliver? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.35,
      "end_seconds": 26.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Six and a half. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.16,
      "end_seconds": 36.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Six and a half, brilliant. Becky, how long has he been bunged up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 38.25,
      "end_seconds": 47.94,
      "duration_seconds": 9.69,
      "text": "I'd say a couple of weeks, but Gran has him most days, so she'd know better."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 48.88,
      "end_seconds": 57.87,
      "duration_seconds": 8.99,
      "text": "Oh, I couldn't say, love. He's been like it a while, months, maybe longer. I didn't write it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.95,
      "end_seconds": 71.69,
      "duration_seconds": 11.74,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll treat it as an on-and-off problem for a while. What are the poos like when they do come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 74.46,
      "end_seconds": 81.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "Hard little pellets, then once a big one that blocks the toilet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.95,
      "end_seconds": 88.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Oliver, does it hurt when you do a poo?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.28,
      "end_seconds": 93.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "No. It doesn't hurt."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 94.04,
      "end_seconds": 103.87,
      "duration_seconds": 9.83,
      "text": "He screams on the toilet, doctor. He holds on to the door and goes red in the face."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 105.22,
      "end_seconds": 110.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "He does, I've heard it from the kitchen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.56,
      "end_seconds": 124.56,
      "duration_seconds": 11.0,
      "text": "I'll write down both what you've said, Oliver, and what Mum and Gran have noticed. Does your tummy hurt at other times?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.88,
      "end_seconds": 129.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Sometimes. Not now. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.14,
      "end_seconds": 135.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Has he ever had an operation, Becky?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 136.85,
      "end_seconds": 140.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "A hernia repair, when he was two."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.63,
      "end_seconds": 143.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Any other health problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 145.11,
      "end_seconds": 148.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Eczema, but it's much better."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.42,
      "end_seconds": 158.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "Okay. I'm going to feel your tummy, Oliver. Lie down on the bed. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.68,
      "end_seconds": 162.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "It tickles. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.3,
      "end_seconds": 188.9,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "His tummy is soft, but I can feel hard lumps low down on the left, which is stool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 190.84,
      "end_seconds": 194.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Is that normal? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.77,
      "end_seconds": 207.64,
      "duration_seconds": 10.87,
      "text": "It tells me the bowel is full. Nothing else looks worrying. His bottom looks normal, no cracks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 208.68,
      "end_seconds": 212.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Can you see the problem? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.62,
      "end_seconds": 219.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Weight 21 kilos, which is right for his age."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 221.98,
      "end_seconds": 225.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "So what's going on? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.44,
      "end_seconds": 240.35,
      "duration_seconds": 12.91,
      "text": "Most likely this is functional constipation, which is very common. I can't rule out an underactive thyroid, but it's less likely."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 241.52,
      "end_seconds": 246.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "What do we do about it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.45,
      "end_seconds": 262.28,
      "duration_seconds": 13.83,
      "text": "First, no medicine today. I'd like you to try more fibre, more water, and regular toilet sits after meals for four weeks, with a sticker chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 263.46,
      "end_seconds": 267.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "I can do stickers at mine. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.84,
      "end_seconds": 274.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Please do. Don't tell him off about accidents. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 277.52,
      "end_seconds": 281.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "And if it's no better? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.03,
      "end_seconds": 289.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "I'll see you again in four weeks, and we'll think about treatment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 290.84,
      "end_seconds": 294.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Four weeks. Thanks, doctor. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.7,
      "end_seconds": 300.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Can I have a sticker now? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.99,
      "end_seconds": 306.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Absolutely. ~"
    }
  ]
}
